"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include a negative surgical margin (0.0), no seminal vesicle invasion (0.0), and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 5.7. Countervailing factors include the documented Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and the absence of lymph node removal, resulting in a pNx status, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. The biopsy finding of Gleason 3+4 is consistent with the surgical specimen. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy difference is not explicitly detailed beyond the overall pathological staging. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data significantly limits the ability to track the trajectory of recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and subsequent changes would be crucial in revising this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 47.33 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 30.76–63.89 months; its coverage has not been validated."
